2. Grain growth: The presence of Si doping can also affect the grain growth behavior of TiO2 nanoparticles. In some cases, it can lead to a decrease in grain growth, as the Si atoms can act as a barrier to the movement of Ti atoms during sintering. In other cases, it can lead to an increase in grain size, as the Si atoms can act as a getter for oxygen vacancies, which can then act as a nucleation site for the formation of larger grains.

