","The concentration of hydronion is \([H_3O^+] = 10^{-4}\) M. The concentration of hydroxide ions is \([OH^-]\). The product of \([H_3O^+]\) and \([OH^-]\) is the ion product of water (\(K_w\)):
\[ K_w = [H_3O^+][OH^-] = 1.8 \times 10^{-14} \text{ M}^2 \]
Solving for \([OH^-]\):
\[ [OH^-] = \frac{1.8 \times 10^{-14}}{10^{-4}} = 1.8 \times 10^{-10} \text{ M} \]
The pH of the solution is:
\[ \text{pH} = -\log[H_3O^+] = -\log(10^{-4}) = 4 \]
The pOH of the solution is:
\[ \text{pOH} = -\log[OH^-] = -\log(1.8 \times 10^{-10}) = 9.74 \]
Since \([H_3O^+] > 10^{-7}\) M, the solution is acidic. 
Thus, \(\text{pH} < 7\), which indicates an acidic solution. 

Final answer: \(\boxed{\text{acidic}}\)",relevance,"# Task Description
