Let's denote the following variables:

- \( C_1 = 0.0125 \, \text{M} \) (concentration of the mixture after mixing)
- \( V_1 = 100 \, \text{mL} \) (volume of the drinking water sample)
- \( C_2 = 0.0125 \, \text{M} \) (concentration of the stock solution)
- \( V_2 = 100 \, \text{mL} \) (volume of the stock solution)
- \( C_0 \) (concentration of the compound in the original drinking water sample)

The mass balance equation for the compound is:

\[
C_0 V_1 + C_2 V_2 = C_1 (V_1 + V_2)
\]

