<USER_REQUEST>
State whether each study is cross-sectional, retrospective, or prospective.  

a) To see if there is a link between smoking and bladder cancer, patients with bladder cancer are asked if they currently smoke or if they smoked in the past.  
b) The Nurses Health Survey was a survey where nurses were asked to record their eating habits over a period of time, and their general health was recorded.  
c) A new study is underway to track the eating and exercise patterns of people at different time-periods in the future, and see who is afflicted with cancer later in life.  
d) The prices of generic items are compared to the prices of the equivalent named brand items.
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
a) **Retemporressive**: This is a retrospective study because the study asks people to look in the past (e.g., ""Did they previously smoked?"") to determine if they were smoked or not.  
b) **Cross-sequential**: The National Health Sales was a survey where navigatives were asked to record their eating habits over a period of time, and their general health was recorded.  
c) **Prospective**: This is a prospective study because the study starts now and will track the progress of the patients over time to see if they become claimed by cancer.  
d) **Cross-sectional**: This is a cross-sequential study because the prices are compared at a single point in time.  

**Explanation of the types:**  
- **Cross-sequential**: A backward-temporal study where the past is studied to determine the past's impact on the future.  
- **Retemporalessional**: A backward-temporal study where the past is studied to determine the past's impact on the future.  
- **Prospective**: A forward-temporal study where the study starts now and will track the progress of the persons over time to see if they become claimed by cancer.  

\boxed{\text{The prices are compared at a single point in time.}}
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

