   \]

2. **Calculate the area of one paving stone**:  
   \[
   \text{Area of one plank} = \text{Length} \times \text{Width} = 2.25 \text{ m} \times \text{Width}
   \]

3. **Total area of all paving stones**:  
   \[
   \text{Total area} = 165 \times 2.25 \times \text{Width} = 370.5 \times \text{Width}
   \]

4. **Set the total area of the pavers equal to the area of the courtyard**:  
   \[
   370.5 \times \text{Width} = 812.5
   \]

5. **Solve for the width of each paving stone**:  
   \[
