Since $a_6 < 0$, we have $19 + 5d < 0 \implies 5d < -19 \implies d < -\frac{19}{5} = -3.8$. 

The 5th term is $a_5 = 19 + (5-1)d = 19 + 4d$. 
The 6th term is $a_6 = 19 + 5d$. 
The 7th term is $a_7 = 19 + 6d$. 

Since the terms become negative starting from the 6th term, $a_5 \geq 0$ and $a_6 < 0$. 
$a_5 = 19 + 4d \geq 0 \implies 4d \geq -19 \implies d \geq -\frac{19}{4} = -4.75$. 

Combining the two inequalities, we have $-4.75 \leq d < -3.8$. Since $d$ is an integer, $d = -4$. 

Thus, the common difference is $-4$. 

The sequence is $a_n = 19 + (n-1)(-4) = 19 - 4n + 4 = 23 - 4n$. 
$a_5 = 23 - 4 \times 5 = 23 - 20 = 3 \geq 0$. 
$a_6 = 23 - 4 \times 6 = 23 - 24 = -1 < 0$. 

The common difference is $-4$. 

