","Let the time spent for each equal time-consuming exercise is $t$ minutes.
Tom starts preparing for the first exercise at 8:00 AM. He spends 20 minutes preparing, so he starts the first exercise at $8:00 + 20 = 8:20$ AM.
The second egg is closed at 10:35 AM. The time spent for the first two eggs is $20 + t + t = 20 + 2t$ minutes.
The second egg is closed at 10:35 AM, so $8:00 + 20 + 2t = 10:35$ AM.
Converting to minutes, $8 \times 60 + 20 + 2t = 10 \times 60 + 35$, so $480 + 20 + 2t = 600 + 35$, which gives $500 + 2t = 635$.
