The limit \( \lim_{h \to 0} \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{1}{h}\right) \) does not exist, as the limit approaches \( \frac{\pi}{2} \) from the right and \( -\frac{\pi}{2} \) from the left. Therefore, \( f'(0) \) does not exist, and \( f(x) \) is not differentiable at \( x = 0 \).

