   The Taylor model assumes that the particles are arranged in a cubic lattice with a center-to-center spacing \(d\). The yield stress is:
   \[
   \sigma_{yr} = \frac{2\pi G b}{d}
   \]
   Substituting the given values:
   \[
   \sigma_{yr} = \frac{2\pi \times 26 \times 10^9 \times 0.286 \times 10^{-9}}{6 \times 10^{-8}} = 0.59 \text{ GN}
   \]

