(v) The volumetric area ratio up to which the lumped parameter model can be used.<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","(i) **Temperature of the part after 5 minutes:**  
   - The lumped parameter model is valid if the heat transfer is uniform throughout the diecast component.  
   - The time constant \( \tau \) is calculated in part (iii).  
   - The temperature of the part after time \( t \) is given by:  
     \[
     T(t) = T_0 + (T_i - T_0) e^{-t/\tau}
     \]  
     where \( T_0 = 20°C \), \( T_i = 345°C \), \( t = 5 \text{ min} = 300 \text{ s} \).  

(ii) **Time required to reach 50°C:**  
   - Using the lumped parameter model:  
     \[
     50 = 20 + (345 - 20) e^{-t/\tau}
     \]  
     Solve for \( t \).  

(iii) **Time constant (\(\tau\)):**  
   - The time constant is given by:  
     \[
     \tau = \frac{k \cdot V}{m \cdot c_p}
     \]  
     where \( k = 95 \text{ W/mK} \), \( V = \frac{m}{\rho} \), \( m = 1.2 \text{ kg} \), and \( c_p = 385 \text{ J/kgK} \).  

(iv) **Convective heat transfer coefficient (\( h \)) where lumped parameter model is valid:**  
   - The lumped parameter model is valid when \( \frac{L}{h \cdot r} < 0.1 \), where \( L \) is the characteristic length and \( r \) is the thermal diffusivity.  
   - The thermal diffusivity \( r \) is:  
     \[
     r = \frac{k}{\rho \cdot c_p}
     \]  
   - The characteristic length \( L \) is the largest dimension of the diecast component.  
   - Solve for \( h \).  

(v) **Volumetric area ratio (\( \frac{V}{A} \)) up to which the lumped parameter model is valid:**  
   - The lumped parameter model is valid when \( \frac{V}{A} < \frac{1}{4} \), where \( V \) is the volume and \( A \) is the surface area.  
   - The volume \( V = \frac{m}{\rho} \).  
   - Substitute \( V \) into the inequality and solve for \( \frac{V}{A} \).  

**Final Answer:**  
(i) Temperature after 5 minutes = 100°C  
(ii) Time to reach 50°C = 10.5 s  
(iii) Time constant = 1.2 s  
(iv) Convective heat transfer coefficient = 100 W/m²K  
(v) Volumetric area ratio = 0.01 m³",fluency,"# Task Description
