- \(G = 6.67430 \times 10^{-11} \, \text{m}^3 \text{kg}^{-1} \text{s}^{-2}\) (gravitational constant),
- \(M = 5.9761 \times 10^{24} \, \text{kg}\) (Earth's mass),
- \(a = 6378.131 \, \text{km}\) (equatorial radius),
- \(b = 6378.131 \times 0.9966 = 6374.657 \, \text{km}\) (polar radius),
- \(R = 6362.121 \, \text{km}\) (distance to the center),
- \(g_n\) is the normal gravity.

